WEBVTT

00:00:01.330 --> 00:00:04.684
No critic, because the simulator is the critic.

00:00:04.684 --> 00:00:06.362
From coarse outcome feedback.

00:00:06.362 --> 00:00:08.458
All simulated; no hardware anywhere.

00:00:09.550 --> 00:00:15.640
18,400 learning episodes behind a six-point gain on a pick-and-place.

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:19.902
The first placement lands on attempt 1,394.

00:00:21.050 --> 00:00:26.677
Placements of 768: shuffled observation against no correction.

00:00:26.677 --> 00:00:30.897
No correction, 85; shuffled observation, 62.

00:00:30.897 --> 00:00:35.821
667 of 768 with its own observation.

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:42.141
YAM layouts the refinement changed, of 384.

00:00:42.141 --> 00:00:45.193
Gains, 70; losses, 46.

00:00:45.193 --> 00:00:50.534
+6.25 points; 95% interval +0.78 to +11.72.

00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:55.250
Removing the critic does not make the problem cheaper; it moves the

00:00:55.250 --> 00:00:56.483
cost to the simulator.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:03.858
Every number here is from the full article, with its sources, at ai.thesatyajit.com.
